# Structured chain-of-thought grammar.
#
# Forces the model's <think> block into a fixed terse structure.
# Source: andthattoo/structured-cot (HumanEval+ result: 22× fewer think
# tokens, +0.6 pp accuracy on Qwen3.6-35B-A3B). For lil/blud agentic
# workloads this is a partly-novel application — paper benched single-turn
# code gen, we're testing multi-turn tool-use.
#
# The think section requires the model to commit to GOAL/APPROACH/EDGE
# before emitting code or any tool call. After </think> any content is
# allowed (so multi-turn tool-call envelopes still work).
#
# llama.cpp GBNF parser quirks: each rule on its own line, hex escapes
# (\x09 \x0A \x0D), no \- or \+ in character classes.

root  ::= think rest
think ::= "<think>\n" "GOAL: " line "APPROACH: " line "EDGE: " line "</think>\n\n"
line  ::= [^\n]+ "\n"
rest  ::= [\x09\x0A\x0D\x20-\x7E]+
